  "notes": [
    "40.1.83 crée deux profils de persistance indépendants : Marché (graphe principal) et Oracle (vue/horizon/zoom/actif/surface).",
    "Le profil Marché est restauré depuis agent_crypto_erith_ia_graph_profile_market_v1 ; au premier boot 40.1.83, la migration préfère last_valid_graph puis workspace_state.",
    "Oracle ne s’ouvre plus automatiquement au rechargement et ses contrôles n’écrivent plus dans agent_crypto_erith_ia_chart_v2_settings_v28_1_17.",
    "Les slots de mémoire restaurent le profil Marché uniquement ; Oracle conserve son propre profil lorsqu’il est ouvert explicitement.",
    "Oracle Evidence/Outcome/Calibration/V2 Shadow et le Window Manager sont inchangés fonctionnellement.",
    "40.1.45: Oracle receives bounded LIVE short-horizon observations, TOP 5 aggregate focus/readout and compact frame-fit title; no synthetic future price is written into historical datasets.",
    "40.1.48: propagation is no longer styled as warning/red; the explicit GitHub propagation text remains visible and true failures remain red/fail.",
    "40.1.48: Math Core header owns the complete Window Manager strip before Dessus/Latéral/Réduire on one line; duplicate bottom placement is removed by moving the same live control node, not cloning it.",
    "40.1.48: Oracle LIVE micro/TOP 5 aggregate functionality is consolidated from the intended 40.1.45 branch; Classic remains untouched.",
    "40.1.50: Math Core state synchronization is consolidated into atlasV2ApplyMathDock; no parallel event bridge or second window implementation remains.",
    "40.1.51: only the native side presentation is compacted; top and floating Math Core keep their existing geometry and controls.",
    "40.1.52: Oracle receives visual-only AUTO/×1/×2/×4 zoom centered on MAINTENANT; no data, score, horizon or mainChart mutation.",
    "40.1.52: Math Core 40.1.50/40.1.51 dock-state and side-header locks are preserved unchanged.",
    "40.1.58: cumulative release includes the 40.1.53 Math Core reduced-rail header suppression restore.",
    "40.1.58: cumulative release includes the 40.1.54 dedicated Oracle view/asset/horizon/zoom persistence and migration.",
    "40.1.58: Oracle calculated outputs and market data remain live/recomputed, never restored from persistence.",
    "Grand Graph is a presentation lock only; Firefox visual validation required.",
    "MIXTE is a safe composite of real main-chart history plus Oracle scenarios in atlasOracleCanvas; it does not inject future points into mainChart.",
    "Premium cumulative candidate. Persistent state includes view, asset, horizon, zoom and surface only; no calculated Oracle output is persisted.",
    "40.1.65: TOP 5 can now remain selected in CONTINUATION; one deterministic composite history is computed from the five normalized real histories and fed to the existing scenario engine.",
    "40.1.66: Oracle Proof compares Always Up, Last Move, Momentum Simple and Top 5 naive baselines with Oracle V1 and Ensemble on the exact same resolved rows; displayed advantage is descriptive only.",
    "40.1.67: the Oracle readout now shows a compact 1m/5m/15m calibration matrix with direction hit-rate, envelope coverage, sample count and Ensemble advantage versus the best naive baseline; all values remain descriptive.",
    "40.1.68: resolved Evidence is now segmented by the regime recorded at T0; each horizon exposes RΔ = Ensemble advantage versus the best naive baseline inside the current regime, on the same Proof sample. No model retuning occurs.",
    "40.1.69: segments stored Ensemble components into same-sample directional performance across 1m/5m/15m and current T0 regime; no live weights change.",
    "40.1.70: derives transparent candidate component weights from resolved historical performance by horizon/regime; candidate weights are displayed but not applied to live Ensemble scores.",
    "40.1.71: adds empirical confidence calibration by active horizon, score-magnitude bucket and regime when sample size permits; data confidence remains separate and no guaranteed probability is claimed.",
    "40.1.72: adds a local read-only Evidence Explorer with filters and latest prediction/outcome rows from IndexedDB; no evidence semantics or market data are rewritten.",
    "40.1.73: adds a visible Oracle Lab dashboard summarizing evidence, outcomes, horizon proof, model performance, regime proof, envelope width and calibrated confidence.",
    "40.1.74: adds local JSON/CSV/Markdown exports and validated JSON merge-import for Oracle Evidence; no network write and no wallet/order action.",
    "40.1.75: audits Evidence timestamps, constituents, quote freshness, duplicate logical observations, overdue pending outcomes and resolution lag; exposes a descriptive quality score without mutating evidence.",
    "40.1.76: adds a prospective Oracle V2 Shadow challenger. Candidate weights are frozen at T0 into new Evidence only; old rows may train candidates but never count as V2 test cases. V2 remains read-only and does not alter Oracle V1 or live Ensemble scores.",
    "40.1.77: surgical Shadow V2 routing fix. Each NEW T0 Evidence row freezes independent 1m/5m/15m challenger snapshots; diagnostics expose eligible/pending/resolved/rejected. No legacy missing horizon is fabricated and no live Oracle score changes.",
    "40.1.83: Workspace Graph Persistence Recovery + Evidence Explorer Header Surgery. A transient empty graph can no longer outrank a coherent last_valid_graph unless Vider was explicitly requested; non-empty selection intent is persisted before chart hydration completes. Oracle Evidence Explorer regains its missing collapse icon and dedicated readable summary grid. Oracle V1/V2, Ensemble, Evidence rows, Math Core and protected Window Manager are unchanged."
